/-!
# KFB: swapping two address bits of a Gaussian array (KFC field moves)

With `q = 2`, KFD's fine field interchange `swapEF` (one `fwdF` and one `bwdF`, linear cost)
swaps two binary fields of the integer array `gflat zs`.  Viewing the Gaussian array of
`W · 2^K` entries as the shape `[W 2^{K-Q-1}, 2, 2^{Q-P-1}, 2, 2^{P+1}]` of integers, the two
binary fields are the index bits `Q > P`.

* `swbit P Q k`: `k` with bits `P` and `Q` interchanged.
* `gflat_gswL`: `gflat (gswL P Q zs) = pull … (swapPos 1 3) … (gflat zs)`.
* `rep_gsw`: on the encoding, the swap of the address bits at positions `P`, `Q` (all roles).
* `gsw_iruns`: the fine IL run.
-/

